ITEMS = ((('what is a fracture and how it happens', 'how do i recognise a fracture', 'what are the signs of fractures', 'what does a fracture look like', 'how can i tell if it is a fracture with a fracture', 'what symptoms occur in fractures', 'how to spot severe fractures', 'what should i look for in a fracture', 'how do i know if fractures are serious', 'what early signs of a fracture are'), 'A fracture is a break in a bone. Signs can include pain, swelling, bruising, inability to use the limb and sometimes a visible deformity. Seek medical assessment and call emergency services if the injury is severe.'), (('what immediate action helps a fracture', 'how do i treat a fracture', 'what is the first aid for fractures', 'how to respond to a fracture', 'what to do immediately in a fracture', 'how do you handle fractures', 'which measures help a fracture', 'how can i assist with a fracture', 'what is the best response to a fracture', 'how should i care for a fracture'), 'For a suspected fracture, keep the person still and support the injured limb in the position found. Cover any wound and call emergency services. Do not try to straighten the limb or move the person unnecessarily.'), (('should i move someone with a fracture', 'how to support a broken arm with a fracture', 'what if the leg is broken with a fracture', 'can i carry a person with fractures', 'how to immobilise an injured limb with a fracture', 'what if the person is in pain with a fracture', 'should i raise the injured limb with a fracture', 'how to protect the joints above and below with a fracture', 'when to call for help with a fracture', 'who can move a casualty safely with a fracture'), 'Avoid moving someone with a fracture unless they are in danger. Support the limb above and below the injury with padding and your hands. Call emergency services and let a qualified person handle movement.'), (('what if a bone is sticking out with a fracture', 'how to cover an open fracture', 'should i push the bone back with a fracture', 'what if there is bleeding around a fracture', 'how to dress the wound with a fracture', 'can i use a sterile dressing with a fracture', 'what if clothing is stuck with a fracture', 'how to protect the skin with a fracture', 'when to call emergency services with a fracture', 'who can treat an open fracture'), 'For an open fracture, cover the wound with a clean dressing and do not push protruding bone back. Apply gentle pressure around the wound to control bleeding. Call emergency services and keep the limb still.'), (('how do i make a sling for a fracture', 'what can i use to support a broken arm with a fracture', 'how to use a triangular bandage with a fracture', 'should i use a scarf with a fracture', 'how tight should a sling be with a fracture', 'what if i have no bandage with a fracture', 'how to check fingers for circulation with a fracture', 'what if the arm is painful with a fracture', 'when to ask for help with a fracture', 'who can show me first aid slings with a fracture'), 'Support a suspected arm fracture with a sling made from a triangular bandage or a broad piece of cloth. Check that fingers stay warm and pink. Ask emergency services for advice and get hands-on training in first aid.'), (('can i give pain relief for a fracture', 'should i give water with a fracture', 'what if the person is hungry with a fracture', 'can i give tablets before hospital with a fracture', 'what if they take regular medicine with a fracture', 'how to keep them comfortable with a fracture', 'what not to give with a fracture', 'when to ask a pharmacist with a fracture', 'how to report medicines to the crew with a fracture', 'who can advise about pain relief with a fracture'), 'Do not give food or drink to someone with a fracture who may need an operation. Ask emergency services before giving any medicine. Keep the person comfortable and tell the crew about regular medication.'), (('how do i know if a bone is broken with a fracture', 'what if there is no deformity with a fracture', 'can a fracture be missed', 'what if the person can still move with a fracture', 'how to tell a fracture from a bruise', 'what if pain is mild with a fracture', 'when to arrange an x ray with a fracture', 'what to tell a doctor with a fracture', 'how urgent is the assessment with a fracture', 'who can diagnose a fracture'), 'A fracture may not look deformed, and a person can sometimes move the limb. If pain, swelling or inability to bear weight persists, seek medical assessment. Only a qualified person with imaging can confirm a break.'), (('what to do for a suspected fracture in a child', 'can children break bones easily with a fracture', "how to check a child's limb with a fracture", 'what if a child will not use an arm with a fracture', 'how to keep a child still with a fracture', 'when to call emergency services for a child fracture', 'what if the child is crying with a fracture', 'how to comfort them with a fracture', 'who can examine a child with a fracture', 'which details to give the doctor about a child fracture'), 'If a child may have a fracture, keep them still and support the limb. Call emergency services for severe deformity, open wounds or significant pain. A doctor can arrange imaging and decide about treatment.'), (('what if a fracture involves the spine or neck', 'should i move someone with back pain with a fracture', 'how to keep the head still with a fracture', 'what if a fall caused the injury with a fracture', 'when to suspect spinal fractures', 'how to support the neck with a fracture', 'what if breathing is affected with a fracture', 'when to call emergency services for a spinal fracture', 'what to tell the operator with a fracture', 'who can manage spinal injuries with a fracture'), 'After a fall or impact, back or neck pain may mean a spinal fracture. Do not move the person unless necessary, support the head and call emergency services. Tell the operator about the mechanism of injury.'), (('when should i call emergency services for a fracture with a fracture', 'is every fracture an emergency', 'what if the limb looks bent with a fracture', 'should i call for a minor break with a fracture', 'what to report about the injury with a fracture', 'how urgent is an open wound with a fracture', 'what if the person is pale with a fracture', 'when to go to hospital yourself with a fracture', 'how to keep the area still with a fracture', 'who takes over fracture care'), 'Call emergency services for a deformed limb, open fracture, severe pain or signs of shock. Tell the operator what happened and which area is injured. Keep the person still and warm until help arrives.'))
